[Music]  Oh Steve Jobs autobiography  hello everybody so today we are going to  talk about 5 tips to increasing your  productivity tip number one leverage the  power of habits to build productive  routines I asked you guys for book  recommendations on Twitter and one of  the books I got was the power of habit  now I actually started listening to the  audiobook of it and I thought it was  really interesting because it helped me  understand how I became more productive  in the past year and now that I can  pinpoint that it was because I was  building a habit out of the things I  wanted to be productive on that I was  able to make a routine and start  cranking out code videos work stuff you  name it now essentially what you want to  do is for the next 21 days do something  every day this could be coding flossing  or whatever you want that you think is  productive and after 21 days it will be  so hard for you to stop that will become  second nature to you tip number two  start multitasking the mundane stuff for  things that doesn't require much  concentration to do do something else  that's more productive while you do that  it would save you surprisingly a lot of  time for example when I clean my room or  do something super boring that I usually  do not like at all I would just you know  whip out an audio book and just start  listening to it and that way I can  actually learn stuff while I do those  mundane tasks another example would be  when I brush my teeth I would read  emails or I would check my social media  accounts and then little by little I'm  actually saving a lot of time in the  long run tip number three keep yourself  busy and accountable with deadlines and  stakeholders now one of the things I  like to do is actually to fill out my  calendar with lots of focus blocks and  deadlines that way I barely have time to  procrastinate the deadlines I set for  myself or even better that I promised to  other people will keep me accountable  for actually completing the projects  that way I can't procrastinate because I  just have a lot to finish and a lot of  people are dependent on me to finish  them  tip number four when taking a break  don't think about work  just have fun this is important because  I see a lot of people half-ass their  productive time but they also have has  their fun time for example I see a lot  of people studying while watching TV  shows that's terrible because you end up  not enjoying the show nor learning the  things are trying to learn so when I  give myself a break I make sure I don't  think about anything else I love TV  shows so I turn off my phone and immerse  myself and surprisingly you'll actually  learn a lot more by doing that like for  example I love to watch kpop videos and  actually learn a lot of cinematography  by dissecting these videos and just  focusing on it but if I was coding while  watching these kpop videos I'd never  appreciate them as much tip number five  exercise exercise exercise now I'm a big  fan of weightlifting so I might be  biased here but I truly believe that  exercising will make you sharper  exercising helps you relieve stress  because it releases endorphins which are  feel-good hormones that way it allows  you to refresh your mind and be a lot  more productive throughout the day it  doesn't even need to be super intense as  long as you get your heart rate up and  work on moving your body more you'll  feel the benefits right away exercise is  a powerful habit and can be a good  primer to you know teaching you to how  to build these productive habits so I  highly recommend going to the gym or  exercising regularly so in conclusion  the most important point I want to get  across is that if you really want to be  good at something or you want to change  an aspect of your life then make it a  habit now you might say oh yeah it's not  as easy as it sounds though and you're  absolutely right you know building  habits extremely hard and I find it hard  myself but if you really care about the  thing you want to achieve then you will  put the effort into it and that's why I  want to keep myself accountable for what  I say and I want you guys to join me so  basically choose something that you  always wanted to do or something that  you want to get good at and together  we'll make it a new habit so for me this  is running I hate running every aspect  of it I'm also extremely bad at it but  that's also why I want to work on it I  want to have better cardio and since I  hate running the most I want to confront  it  and if I can make running a habit then  it gives me the confidence that in the  future I can make anything a habit I  also want to thank audible for  sponsoring this video and I wanted to  also recommend the audio book the power  of habit which I talked a lot about in  this video and when you sign up for a  free 30-day trial inaudible today at  audible.com slash Joma you can go and  get that audio book that book really  helped me become more productive and  deconstruct the idea of habits and it's  great because now why I run this summer  I can listen to it so I don't need to  sit down and have a dedicated reading  time they also have a huge library of  other audiobooks you can listen to so if  you want to get a free 30-day trial you  can get it at audible.com slash Joma or  you can text Joma  to 500 500 so thank you audible again  for allowing me to make this video and I  hope you guys enjoyed it and don't  forget to smash that like button and  subscribe please  [Music]  because it goes through the holes you  keep sleeping on the couch

